    "done_when": "Deliver §6 of docs/plans/lane-and-model-routing.html exactly as that section states, following the pattern §3 used for claude. §3's validated artifact and report are in ~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/claude-lane-collapse/, and the dotfiles host flight now carries lanes.claude. The plan and its locked decisions are the authority.\n\n1. Host flight, as a validated artifact. Do not edit the dotfiles repository. Copy the live /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/dotfiles/reckon/flight.yaml into your report directory as flight.before.yaml. Write flight.yaml beside it, moving codex-astra and codex-luna into lanes.codex.models with sol as the default model and retiring their backend blocks, exactly as §3 did for claude. Keep the names declared if §1's expansion needs them to derive the legacy entries. codex-terra stays retired; its alias resolves only for history. Keep every other block and comment byte-identical.\n2. Catalogue, in this worktree. In docs/state/reckon/model-catalogue.yaml, retire the codex-astra and codex-luna backends blocks wherever the lanes.codex declaration now carries them, with the same keep-the-name rule.\n3. Validate with the main checkout's reckon (/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python), passing host_path and catalogue_path to reckon.flight.resolve, or setting RECKON_FLIGHT_CONFIG for the host file. For the shipped scope and every project in ~/.config/reckon/mounts.json, the resolved config changes only by the lane annotations the expansion adds: lane, model_key, derived_from and the lanes block. Nothing else may be changed or removed. Keep a per-scope log ending in an EXIT line. --backend codex with model astra, or the derived codex-astra entry, resolves to the same model, effort and argv as the retired codex-astra block; check codex-luna the same way.\n4. Negative control: changing astra's effort in the lane declaration makes the codex-astra equivalence check fail.\n\nDeliver flight.before.yaml, flight.yaml, flight.diff, the logs and report.md in your report directory, and commit the catalogue change in this worktree with a conventional subject and a body. Gate: the scope comparison and equivalence logs, plus tests/test_catalogue_declares_lanes.py and every tests/test_flight*.py, run with PATH=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin:$PATH /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, base and head, each log ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta.",
